It is evening, and it is getting dark.
A lamp stands by the window.
I try to turn it on.
But the bulb doesn't work, so the living room is still dark.
I am hungry and go out into the kitchen.
I open the cupboard to make dinner.
But the cupboard is empty.
There is no food and no coffee.
My bag is standing by the door.
I look in it.
Luckily I have a little money in the bag.
"I'll just pop down to the shop," I say to myself.
I put my coat on again.
Then I walk out of my new apartment.
